    2  A   ablation_onset           0.858    85.42   3.922e+06  stylized
          Net heating flux first exceeds radiative loss at T_ablate = 2300 K, so ablation switches on
          (a kink in the slope). Real onset is gradual over a few km. BELOW this point the model's
          light is drag work only (no ablated material): treat light above ~85 km as low-confidence.
          Loosely like the end of Phase 1 / start of Phase 2 in [R22], but the model has no spin,
          volatile (Na/K) emission or melt physics.
    3  Y   first_yield              3.351    42.95   3.818e+09  physical
          Loading rho v^2 reaches S0 = 1 MPa. The body starts to flatten (pancake): area, drag and
          heating all grow, so the light rises faster. Analogue of the onset of fragmentation (Phase 5
          / H_f in [R22]).
    4  F   flare                    3.408    41.97   1.119e+10  stylized
          Light rises x19.8 in 0.18 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated
          with: yield gen 0 at 42.9 km (99% of m0); split gen 0 at 41.2 km (98% of m0); yield gen 1 at
          40.1 km (37% of m0). Dust groups supply 80% of the rise and 76% of the light at the end of
          the flare. A real fragmentation flare (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come
          from the model's deterministic cascade.
    5  B   first_breakup            3.450    41.26   2.152e+10  stylized
          Spread factor reached f_split = 2: the body breaks into 4 children plus 20 % of its mass as
